{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nRelease maintainers read docs/releasing.md to know what a release produces. Its \"Tag signing — SKIPPED\" section (docs/releasing.md:564-571) says rebar keeps **annotated** tags, but the tags release.yml creates are lightweight, so the runbook misdescribes the release record.\n\n## Observation (2026-11-09, rechecked 2026-11-18)\n- docs/releasing.md, section 'Tag signing — SKIPPED (annotated tags + attestations instead)', says rebar keeps annotated release tags.\n- `gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/git/ref/tags/<tag>` returns object type `commit` (a lightweight tag) for v0.13.1, v0.14.0, v0.15.0, v0.15.1 and v0.16.0.\n- The tag is created by release.yml's `github_release` job via `gh release create \"$TAG\" --target \"$SHA\" ...` (.github/workflows/release.yml:323); the comment above it already says `gh` \"creates the lightweight dispatch-version tag\".\n- `gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/immutable-releases` returns `{\"enabled\":true}`, so the doc's \"immutable releases on\" claim holds.\n- The same \"Release-policy decisions\" block's RC-safety note (docs/releasing.md:580-585) still describes a tag-triggered release (\"`release.yml` fires on **all** `v*` tags\", \"a hypothetical `v1.0.0rc1` tag\", \"No rc-form tag may be pushed\", \"detect `rc` in the tag\"). release.yml's `on:` is only `workflow_dispatch` with a `version` input (release.yml:18-24), and release.yml:4 says pushed tags cannot start a release. `scripts/release_guards.py` has no `rc` handling, and release.yml:323 passes `--latest` unconditionally.\n\n## Approach\nDecision: the docs are wrong; the workflow is right. Reasoning, recorded here and in the doc:\n- Release provenance in rebar comes from PEP 740 attestations signed by the Trusted Publishing OIDC identity (`attestations: true` in the `publish` job) and from GitHub immutable releases, as the same doc section already states. An unsigned annotated tag adds only a tagger name, date and message written by the workflow's own bot identity; nothing can verify it, so it adds no provenance.\n- The section's own peer baseline says ruff/uv/httpx use lightweight tags.\n- Producing an annotated tag would add a separate git-objects API call (or a checkout with push credentials) to the post-publish job, more privileged surface for no verification gain.\nSo:\n1. Rewrite the \"Tag signing\" section heading to \"Tag signing — SKIPPED (lightweight tags + attestations instead)\" and its text to say release tags are **lightweight** tags created by `gh release create` at the released SHA, keep the revisit triggers, and say that if tags ever need to be verifiable they must be signed (an unsigned annotated tag does not help).\n2. Rewrite the whole RC-safety note in terms of the dispatch input, because the release is dispatch-only: release.yml takes its version from `inputs.version`, passes `--latest` unconditionally and runs the MCP-registry job, so dispatching an rc-form version (e.g. `-f version=1.0.0rc1`) would mark it Latest and publish it to the MCP registry. Rule: **no rc-form version may be dispatched** unless release.yml first gains a prerelease guard that detects `rc` in `inputs.version`, passes `--prerelease` instead of `--latest`, and skips the MCP-registry job. The PEP 440 spelling note stays. The rule itself (no rc releases without a guard) is unchanged; only its trigger wording is corrected.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/releasing.md` — the \"Tag signing\" section and the whole RC-safety note in \"Release-policy decisions\".\n- `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py` — one test tying the doc's tag type and RC note to the workflow.\n\n## Testing\n- New test `test_docs_tag_type_matches_workflow`, written first and seen failing against the current doc: release.yml's `github_release` job creates the tag with `gh release create` and release.yml contains no `git tag -a`; docs/releasing.md contains the heading \"Tag signing — SKIPPED (lightweight tags + attestations instead)\", does not contain \"keep **annotated** tags\", and does not contain the tag-trigger phrases \"fires on **all** `v*` tags\" or \"No rc-form tag may be pushed\".\n- `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] docs/releasing.md and release.yml agree on the tag type: either the doc states lightweight tags, or github_release creates an annotated tag. Checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py -k tag_type` passes on merged main.\n- [ ] The RC-safety note describes the dispatch trigger (`inputs.version`), not tag pushes. Checked: the same test passes, and reading the merged note.\n- [ ] The reasoning for choosing lightweight tags is recorded on this ticket and in docs/releasing.md. Checked: reading the merged doc section.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795034247573018338,"uuid":"354d2cc1-3552-4407-9600-53a609ce4116"}